(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[15 1 "// The AOT's side of the runtime (PY8; doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md §7, PYS13 (a); doc/python/PYI-SPEC.md"] [16 1 "// §10): arbace.python.aot translates each code object's IR into a Go function over this package, a"] [17 1 "// compiled interpreter: the instructions become Go statements calling the helpers below with their"] [18 1 "// arguments as constants, the jumps gotos, the decoding and the dispatch loop's switch gone. The"] [19 1 "// frame stays the machine's heap frame (its stack, locals, cells, PC and Lasti), so a compiled"] [20 1 "// function is run by the same loop (Thread.run) in place of step: a call of a Python function still"] [21 1 "// pushes the callee's frame (the Go stack never holds Python frames, RecursionError where CPython"] [22 1 "// raises it), an exception unwinds by the code's exception table, and a generator's or coroutine's"] [23 1 "// frame is resumed by the function's entry switch on its PC (a state machine over the heap frame)."] [24 1 "//"] [25 1 "// A compiled program registers its modules' IR (the loader's text) with their native functions in"] [26 1 "// pre-order (the code object, then its nested code objects in constant order); the loader attaches"] [27 1 "// them (ReadIR's irLoadedHook). Source compiled at run time (exec, eval, compile, an import of a module"] [28 1 "// not compiled ahead) goes to the host's compiler (PYI_AOT_COMPILER, arbace.python.aot compile-server)"] [29 1 "// and runs on the dispatch loop."] [32 41 "// AotKey(mode, source) -> the IR text compiled ahead"] [33 41 "// the IR text -> its code objects' native functions"] [39 1 "// AotKey is the key of a source text compiled ahead in mode (exec, eval, single): its SHA-256 in hex."] [45 1 "// AotRegister registers a module compiled ahead: key its source's (AotKey; \"\" for the main module,"] [46 1 "// which AotMain runs from its text), ir its IR text, natives its code objects' functions in pre-order."] [54 1 "// aotAttach is ReadIR's hook: the native functions of a registered IR text set on its code objects."] [78 1 "// aotCompile is a compiled program's compiler (SetCompiler): a source compiled ahead, else the host's."] [94 1 "// hostCompile asks the host's compiler (the command PYI_AOT_COMPILER names, started once: arbace.python.aot"] [95 1 "// compile-server) for source's IR: a request \"MODE\\tFILE\\tBYTES\\n\" and the source, an answer \"BYTES\\n\""] [96 1 "// and the compiler's text (arbace.python.run/compile-source's: the IR, SyntaxError: ..., incomplete)."] [147 1 "// AotMain is a compiled program's process: sys.argv and sys.path as bin/pyi run gives them, the"] [148 1 "// compiler of source at run time, the main module's IR run as __main__ (RunModule); the exit status."] [149 1 "// PYI_AOT_STATS names a file for the code objects run compiled and on the loop, and the host's compiles."] [165 1 "// AotBadPC is a compiled function entered at a PC that is not an instruction's."] [170 1 "// The helpers of the compiled code: each is an operation of step's switch (eval.go) with its argument"] [171 1 "// a constant; the ones that may raise return the error, a call also a *pushFrame."] [358 1 "// AotToBool is to-bool (not false) and not (not true)."] [495 1 "// AotForIter is for-iter: the next item pushed (false), or at the end the iterator popped (true)."] [500 22 "// FOR_ITER clears a raised StopIteration: the loop's end"] [513 1 "// AotTruthy is the popped value's truth (the conditional jumps')."] [547 1 "// AotCall is call [N KWNAMES] (kw the kwnames tuple's constant index, or -1): a Python function's"] [548 1 "// frame pushed (the *pushFrame returned: f.PC must be the next instruction's), a generator made, or"] [549 1 "// any other callable called."] [609 1 "// AotExec runs instruction i of f's code as step runs it, for the operations the compiled code does not"] [610 1 "// spell out: the rarer ones of step's switch and every operation another file registers (RegisterOp)."] [611 1 "// f.PC is the next instruction's when it is called; an operation that jumps sets it."] [743 1 "// AotPopIsNone pops the top and tells whether it is None (jump-if-none, jump-if-not-none)."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[62 32] [80 47] [108 42] [110 40] [124 86] [139 41] [158 36] [249 41] [262 36] [282 57] [402 12] [402 28] [403 40] [415 22] [480 25] [480 33] [499 28] [564 47] [569 35] [620 29] [628 62] [633 24] [636 62] [643 44] [650 29] [660 17] [660 31] [664 22] [664 30] [675 37] [694 30]]} (go/file "aot.go" :imports [


